---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import comparison from "../data/decision-comparison.json";
import example from "../data/decision-comparison-example.json";

const formatCost = (value: number | null) => value === null ? "Unknown" : `$${value.toFixed(6)}`;
---

<Base title="Verdict — decision-model comparison" description="A dated synthetic support-ticket comparison of Jev Direct, Clef, Clef Flash, and GPT-5.4 Nano.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Verdict internal evaluation · Recorded October 2, 2026</p>
  <h1>Four models. The same 24 tickets.</h1>
  <p class="tagline">
    Jev Direct, Clef, Clef Flash, and Nano each chose the expected team on all 24
    tickets. This run shows their observed response time and cost; it does not
    identify a decision-quality winner.
  </p>
  <p><a class="playground-link" href="/playground">Try your own decision →</a></p>

  <section class="recorded-example" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
    <p class="example-label">One recorded example · {example.item_id} · mixed request</p>
    <h2 id="example-heading">Which team should handle this ticket?</h2>
    <p class="table-note">Question summary: choose the team for the primary requested action.
      <a href="#shared-policy">Read the full policy</a>.</p>
    <h3>Allowed answers</h3>
    <div class="case-tags">{comparison.answers.map((answer) => <span>{answer}</span>)}</div>
    <h3>Ticket input</h3>
    <blockquote>{example.context}</blockquote>
    <p><strong>Expected answer: <span class="good">{example.expected}</span></strong></p>
    <p class="table-note">{example.explanation}</p>
    <h3>Recorded model choices</h3>
    <dl class="example-results">
      {example.responses.map((response) => <div>
        <dt>{comparison.providers.find((provider) => provider.id === response.provider)?.name}</dt>
        <dd class="good">{response.answer}</dd>
      </div>)}
    </dl>
    <p class="table-note">An original synthetic benchmark item from this run, with labels authored
      by Verdict. These are saved responses; opening this page makes no model calls.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="run-facts" aria-label="Run overview">
    <div><strong>{comparison.n_cases}</strong><span>unique synthetic tickets</span></div>
    <div><strong>{comparison.n_calls}</strong><span>live calls · no retries or cache</span></div>
    <div><strong>{comparison.providers.reduce((total, provider) => total + provider.errors, 0)}</strong><span>errors across all four models</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Observed results</h2>
  <p class="table-note">Each model answered {comparison.n_cases} tickets. Cost below is the total for
    those {comparison.n_cases} calls per model, not the cost of the single example above.
    Estimates and reported charges are labeled separately.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Decision comparison results" tabindex="0">
    <table class="board comparison-board">
      <caption class="sr-only">Results from the October 2, 2026 synthetic support-ticket run</caption>
      <thead><tr>
        <th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Correct / attempted</th>
        <th scope="col">Errors</th><th scope="col">Median wall time</th>
        <th scope="col">Total cost / {comparison.n_cases} calls</th><th scope="col">Cost basis</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {comparison.providers.map((provider) => <tr>
          <th scope="row">{provider.name}</th>
          <td class="num good">{provider.correct} / {provider.attempted}</td>
          <td class="num">{provider.errors}</td>
          <td class="num">{Math.round(provider.median_wall_ms)} ms</td>
          <td class="num">{formatCost(provider.cost_usd)}</td>
          <td>{provider.cost_basis}</td>
        </tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">
    Wall time includes network and adapter processing. Every call had a usable
    reported or estimated cost; costs were not reconciled against invoices.
  </p>

  <h2>What these tickets test</h2>
  <p>
    Six examples per team: billing, technical, account, and other. Cases include
    mixed requests, misleading keywords, negation, embedded instructions,
    paraphrases, and an underspecified request. The labels were authored with the
    examples, rather than independently assigned by support staff.
  </p>
  <div class="case-tags" aria-label="Case categories">
    {comparison.categories.map((category) => <span>{category}</span>)}
  </div>
  <details id="shared-policy">
    <summary>Read the shared routing policy</summary>
    <p>{comparison.question}</p>
  </details>

  <p class="callout">
    All four passed this set. It is still too easy to separate decision quality.
    One call per provider and ticket, fixed ordering, and network variability do
    not establish stable speed rankings. Passing these injection examples does
    not establish general injection resistance. Confidence is not validated here.
  </p>

  <details>
    <summary>Models and run details</summary>
    <ul class="model-list">
      {comparison.providers.map((provider) => <li>
        <strong>{provider.name}</strong>: requested <code>{provider.requested_model}</code>;
        reported <code>{provider.reported_models.join(", ")}</code>.
      </li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>Sequential calls, fixed provider order, no client retries, cache, fallback, or escalation.
      Jev/Clef used typed questions; Nano used a structured-output chat prompt.
      All received the same question, labels, and ticket text. Reported model IDs
      are provider-supplied; Clef identifiers do not specify dated snapshots.</p>
    <p class="updated">Run started: {comparison.started_at} (UTC).</p>
    <p class="fingerprint">Case fingerprint: <code>{comparison.dataset_sha256}</code></p>
    <p>Original synthetic case definitions are in <code>python/scripts/compare_decisions.py</code>.
      Full request/response evidence is retained locally; this page publishes aggregate results
      and the recorded choices for {example.item_id}.</p>
  </details>

  <p class="next-note">
    Looking for the previous suite results? <a href="/historical">View the historical leaderboard</a>.
    This comparison is separate from that snapshot. <a href="/methodology">Read the methodology</a>
    or <a href="/playground">try your own decision</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<script>
  const sharedPolicy = document.getElementById("shared-policy");
  const openLinkedPolicy = () => {
    if (location.hash === "#shared-policy" && sharedPolicy instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) {
      sharedPolicy.open = true;
    }
  };
  document.querySelector('a[href="#shared-policy"]')?.addEventListener("click", openPolicy);
  function openPolicy() {
    if (sharedPolicy instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) sharedPolicy.open = true;
  }
  window.addEventListener("hashchange", openLinkedPolicy);
  openLinkedPolicy();
</script>

<style>
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-2); margin: 30px 0 0; font-size: 13px; }
  h1 { margin-top: 8px; }
  .playground-link { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .recorded-example { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px; margin: 26px 0; }
  .example-label { color: var(--accent-2); font-size: 13px; margin: 0; }
  .recorded-example h2 { margin-top: 10px; }
  .recorded-example h3 { font-size: 14px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
  .recorded-example .case-tags { margin: 8px 0; }
  blockquote { margin: 0; padding: 16px; background: var(--bg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .example-results { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
  .example-results > div { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; }
  .example-results dt { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .example-results dd { margin: 6px 0 0; font-weight: 600; }
  .run-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin: 26px 0; }
  .run-facts > div { border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--panel); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; }
  .run-facts strong { display: block; font-size: 26px; }
  .run-facts span, .table-note, .next-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 12px; }
  .table-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .comparison-board th { cursor: default; }
  .comparison-board tbody th { color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: normal; }
  .comparison-board th:last-child, .comparison-board td:last-child { text-align: left; }
  .case-tags { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 18px 0; }
  .case-tags span { color: var(--muted); padding: 4px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; font-size: 12px; }
  details { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin: 16px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  details p, .model-list { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .model-list li { margin: 10px 0; }
  details code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .fingerprint code { word-break: break-all; }
  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .recorded-example { padding: 16px; }
    .example-results { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .run-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .run-facts > div { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 16px; }
    .run-facts strong { min-width: 36px; }
  }
</style>
